A||N||8||JasonC||Bleeder Tool question||||5||
Z||000000||JasonC||01-31-2001||06:15 PM||||Any have a <I>ONE MAN BRAKE BLEEDER</I> tool? There is one at the Fiero store and I've seen them for sale at a store or two. <P>I sometimes don't have access to a partner to push a pedal and this looks like it might make it so I don't need a pedal pusher. I'm just looking for opinions of it's use.<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Jason Carmichael<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net2/smile-r.gif"> <A HREF="http://www.getpaid2surf.net/97GPGT" TARGET=_blank>My GP GT on the net.</A> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net2/smile-l.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||lawrence||01-31-2001||06:56 PM||||You can buy them at <A HREF="http://www.speedbleeder.com." TARGET=_blank>www.speedbleeder.com.</A>   Or, you can make something similar.  Here's what I did:<P> <A HREF="http://www.webelectricmagazine.com/98/4/bleeder.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.webelectricmagazine.com/98/4/bleeder.htm</A> <P>Good luck,<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://www.webelectricmagazine.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.webelectricmagazine.com</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/products" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/products</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||JasonC||01-31-2001||09:28 PM||||Ok, one question on your home made jobby. When you take off the assembly to put back the regular one, what keeps the system from getting air now? Just because it's the top?||||reg||6
Z||000003||RossT||01-31-2001||11:30 PM||||I recently bought a "mighty vac" from <A HREF="http://www.harborfreight.com" TARGET=_blank>www.harborfreight.com</A>   I bought the best one they had, and man i did all four brakes and the clutch in about an hour or two. The fluid looked like, well you know what.  That tool also many more applications.  Well worth 50 bucks.||||reg||1
Z||000004||2birds||02-01-2001||06:36 AM||||My Mity-vac only cost me $25 at WalMart, and it was well worth it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||02-01-2001||10:33 AM||||i have been unable to succesfully make my mity vac work.  perhaps i need to read the directions again.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000006||2birds||02-01-2001||04:55 PM||||bhooper,<P>I hooked up one hose from the bleeder screw to the jar (the connection that goes to the tiny hose leading to the bottom of the jar) and the other hose from the connection at the top of the jar to to the mity-vac suction port.  draw a vacuum,, being careful not to collapse the hoses, then crack the bleeder screw until fluid flows out.  Repeat until no more bubbles appear in the first hose or jar.  <BR>The jar, with fluid covering the bottom of the tiny hose, works like a loop seal in your toilet (or a bong if that's your style), to prevent air from flowing back into the brake or clutch hydraulic system.<BR>You should never get any fluid in the second hose.<BR>  The only problem I've ever had is air leaking past the threads in theh bleeder screw or between the hose and the bleeder screw.  I little grease sometimes fixes that.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||lawrence||02-02-2001||12:20 PM||||The fluid runs downhill, so when you take the bleeder out, fluid will come out of the hole.<P>Good luck,<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://www.webelectricmagazine.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.webelectricmagazine.com</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/products" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/products</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Greg Piet||02-02-2001||12:41 PM||||Hoop,<BR>Dont feel bad I never got mine to work either...<P>I got a 3.99 brake bleeder that worked wonders.  It was  just a tube with a spring loaded ball bearing.<BR>Loosen the caliper bleeder just barely enough to allow fluid to escape.  Press on brake which opened the bleeder ball bearing, then closed when brake pressure reduced.<P>As long as one had the caliper bleeder on tight enough so that air didnt get in through the threads it worked great, but could be tricky to get the caliper port loose enough to bleed, but not too loose.<P>I still have yet to find a better way than how my pappy showed me many many moons ago.||||reg||1
